  "context": {
    "context": "SKETCH: No proof is expected here in one piece: propose a cut into smaller statements. One move is known to keep size and function: a wire that is below the function and feeds an OR gate can be moved to the output (delete that OR, add one OR at the top). Repeating it ends with a circuit that is an OR of blocks, no wire inside a block being below the function. The open part is a least circuit whose blocks are not single stars: such a block must be shown to cost at least a star cover of the edges it accepts. No sorry, no new axiom. Own namespace for every declaration.",
    "dead": [],
    "sketch": "No proof is expected here in one piece: propose a cut into smaller statements. One move is known to keep size and function: a wire that is below the function and feeds an OR gate can be moved to the output (delete that OR, add one OR at the top). Repeating it ends with a circuit that is an OR of blocks, no wire inside a block being below the function. The open part is a least circuit whose blocks are not single stars: such a block must be shown to cost at least a star cover of the edges it accepts. No sorry, no new axiom. Own namespace for every declaration.",
    "title": "On a plane of order q, every fan-in-two AND/OR circuit for incidence can be replaced by a read-2 one with at most as many gates",
